Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 04:43:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Show a video only from a whole first frame

- A video frame is copied into its texture while its buffer's lock is
  held. The first frame was only pointed at and copied when the texture
  was first drawn, after the lock was let go: by then the player could be
  writing the next frame into that buffer, and the texture got a frame
  half new, half old (the rest of a black start), which stayed until the
  next frame.
- The texture keeps no pointer to the player's buffers (it was read
  again when the texture was reloaded, also after the buffers were
  freed); a frame of another size makes the texture again.
- The video replaces the snapshot only once its first frame is in the
  texture.
---
 es-core/src/components/VideoVlcComponent.cpp | 66 +++++++++++++-------
 es-core/src/components/VideoVlcComponent.h   |  1 +
 es-core/src/resources/TextureData.cpp        | 19 ++++--
 3 files changed, 59 insertions(+), 27 deletions(-)

